{:edb/db-before-t 2055 :edb/db-after-t 2056 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535368 50 #inst "2026-10-08T22:56:45.081Z" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078258 1100 "Consider the equation $y''-3y'-4y = 0$ where $y=y(t)$. If $y = e^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then what is $\\lambda$?" 13194139535368 false] [17592186078258 1100 "Consider the equation $y''-3y'-4y = 0$ where $y=y(t).$ If $y = e^{\\lambda t}$ is a solution, then what is $\\lambda?$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078258 1145 "Assuming\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nand differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda t},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λt} - 3λe^{λt} - 4e^{λt} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λt}(λ^{2} - 3λ - 4) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\lambda^2 - 3\\lambda - 4 = 0\n$$\n\nFactoring, we get\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4) (\\lambda +1) = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = 4$ and\n\n$$\n\\lambda = -1\n$$" 13194139535368 false] [17592186078258 1145 "Assuming $y=e^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda t},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}-3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-4{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\lambda^2 -  3\\lambda - 4 = 0\n$$\n\nFactoring, we get\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4) (\\lambda +1) = 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = 4$ and $\\lambda =  -1.$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078259 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + \\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} - 2y =0.\n$$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078259 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n$\\frac{\\textrm{d}^2 y}{\\textrm{d} x^2} + \\frac{\\textrm{d} y}{\\textrm{d} x} - 2y =0$." 13194139535368 false] [17592186078259 1145 "This is a second-order homogeneous ODE. So, we assume the solutions take the form\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\lambda e^{\\lambda x}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2} = \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λx} + λe^{λx} - 2e^{λx} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λx}(λ^{2} + λ - 2) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2} + λ - 2 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ - 1)(λ + 2) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = 1$ and\n\n$$\n\\lambda = -2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{x} + Be^{-2 x}\n$$" 13194139535368 false] [17592186078259 1145 "This is a second-order homogeneous ODE. So, we assume the solutions take the form $y=e^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\lambda e^{\\lambda x}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2} = \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = 1$ and $\\lambda = -2.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{x} + Be^{- 2 x}.\n$$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078260 1100 "Given that $y = y(x)$ satisfies the equation $y''+7y'+6y = 0$, which of the following could **not** be $y(x)$?\n\n1. $-3e^{-6x}$\n2. $2e^{-6x}-4e^{-x}$\n3. $e^{-6x}+2e^{x}$" 13194139535368 false] [17592186078260 1100 "Given that $y = y(x)$ satisfies the equation $y''+7y'+6y = 0,$ which of the following could **not** be $y(x)?$\n\n- $-3e^{-6x}$\n\n- $2e^{-6x}-4e^{-x}$\n\n- $e^{-6x}+2e^{x}$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186078260 1145 "This is a second-order homogeneous ODE. So, we assume the solutions take the form\n\n$$\ny=e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda x},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2}e^{λx} + 7λe^{λx} + 6e^{λx} &= 0 \\\\\ne^{λx}(λ^{2} + 7λ + 6) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ^{2} + 7λ + 6 &= 0 \\\\\n(λ + 6)(λ + 1) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the characteristic equation are\n\n$$\n\\lambda = -6\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{-6x} + Be^{-x}\n$$\n\nFinally, we need to determine whether each of the given functions takes the form shown above.\n\n- Function I takes the above form with $A=-3$ and $B=0$. So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n- Function II takes the above form with $A=2$ and $B=-1$. So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n- Function III does *not* take the above form. It contains $e^x$, which is not included in the above form. So, it is *not* a solution to the given ODE.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535368 false] [17592186078260 1145 "This is a second-order homogeneous ODE. So, we assume the solutions take the form $y=e^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\ny'= \\lambda e^{\\lambda x},\\qquad y''= \\lambda^2 e^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+7\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+6{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +6) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)(\\lambda +1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the characteristic equation are $\\lambda = -6$ and $\\lambda = - 1.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny = Ae^{-6x} + Be^{- x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we need to determine whether each of the given functions takes the form shown above.\n\n- Function I takes the above form with $A=-3$ and $B=0.$ So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n\n- Function II takes the above form with $A=2$ and $B=-1.$ So, it is a solution to the given ODE.\n\n- Function III does *not* take the above form. It contains $e^x,$ which is not included in the above form. So, it is *not* a solution to the given ODE.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535368 true] [17592186078413 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346101 13194139535368 true] [17592186078413 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346129 13194139535368 true] [17592186078413 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346150 13194139535368 true] [17592186078413 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346157 13194139535368 true] [17592186078413 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346164 13194139535368 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346108 13194139535368 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346136 13194139535368 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346143 13194139535368 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346171 13194139535368 true] [17592186078414 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346178 13194139535368 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346115 13194139535368 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346122 13194139535368 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346185 13194139535368 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346192 13194139535368 true] [17592186078415 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346199 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346102 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1089 "q-129836" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1100 "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-{y}^{′}-2y=0$ where $y=y(x).$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution, then $\\lambda =$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1113 #uuid "724b6c69-206a-5ea4-83bf-7187a1c59529" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346101 1145 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =2.$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346103 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346104 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346105 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346106 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346107 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1041 "selection" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346106 13194139535368 true] [17592186346102 1110 #uuid "b6040974-ff1c-500d-9a34-66eb2519d2a4" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346103 1034 "$-1$ or $1$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535368 true] [17592186346103 1111 #uuid "9afe31ce-c923-562f-b7b6-2d3d698a875e" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346104 1034 "$-2$ or $1$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535368 true] [17592186346104 1111 #uuid "6518dc53-ddad-5ce4-b6e6-bdf04d67e24c" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346105 1034 "$-2$ or $2$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535368 true] [17592186346105 1111 #uuid "3f97654d-23d5-59f2-bb05-4609daf7f8cf" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346106 1034 "$-1$ or $2$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535368 true] [17592186346106 1111 #uuid "9529f504-7dd7-5213-b1ed-5528511e8cd9" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346107 1034 "$1$ or $2$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535368 true] [17592186346107 1111 #uuid "a762a1f9-f24a-56aa-b58a-325678b55ec7" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346109 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1089 "q-130114" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y=0.\n$$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1113 #uuid "a00e000f-0aed-57ad-bae8-b7c74a96c1be" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346108 1145 "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-2{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =1.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346110 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346111 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346112 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346113 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346114 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1041 "selection" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346111 13194139535368 true] [17592186346109 1110 #uuid "9f8532be-437d-5493-9833-0fba12a1d94e" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346110 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{2x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346110 1111 #uuid "88370a28-bf5c-513d-aec1-6d976995c1bf" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346111 1034 "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346111 1111 #uuid "01eab8b3-c7d0-545f-ba47-6cd7069890d8" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346112 1034 "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346112 1111 #uuid "c5558a64-a793-5309-9748-ca339be72344" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346113 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346113 1111 #uuid "409d5a08-2768-5997-a884-4725a7abc6fa" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346114 1034 "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346114 1111 #uuid "cc1498fd-9670-5c71-b89c-0afee33afc14" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346116 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1089 "q-130123" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1100 "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+3y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1113 #uuid "82e16a64-d25e-5283-bcae-ba7d724711ba" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346115 1145 "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+4\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =-1.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-3x}$ and ${e}^{-x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{3x}$ is not a solution." 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346117 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346118 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346119 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346120 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346121 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1041 "selection" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346119 13194139535368 true] [17592186346116 1110 #uuid "f3ad6c93-0fe9-5aee-ac8b-fee5245535bf" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346117 1034 "3{e}^{-x}" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346117 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535368 true] [17592186346117 1111 #uuid "48c591be-bc14-50bb-ad87-4399f05b4b09" 13194139535368 true] [17592186346118 1034 "{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{-x}" 131941